# ============================================================================
# ALLOWLIST .gitignore — deny everything, then admit the audio estate.
#
# This repository is rooted at the CLAUDE folder, which is a 2.9 GB working
# directory holding video, photography, scripts, HAR captures and a decade of
# unrelated work. The audio estate inside it is about 5 MB. A denylist would
# be a list of every mistake somebody thought of in advance; this is the other
# way round, and the only files git can see are the ones named below.
#
# TWO THINGS IN THIS FOLDER MUST NEVER BE COMMITTED, and the leading `*` is
# what guarantees it rather than the explicit rules further down:
#   - www.patreon.com*.har — browser captures containing session_id,
#     authorization and cookie values. A live login in plaintext.
#   - the video and image files, which are hundreds of megabytes each.
#
# Verify, do not trust. After any edit here:
#     git status --porcelain            # must list ONLY estate paths
#     git check-ignore -v www.patreon.com.har
#     du -sh $(git ls-files | head -1000)
# ============================================================================

# --- deny everything, including directory contents -------------------------
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes

# --- admit the estate ------------------------------------------------------
!/shared/
!/AUTOPSY/
!/RIGOR/
!/CASKET/
# PALLBEARER, the physically modelled bass, joined 2026-08-18. It depends on
# ../shared/necromath, so like the other three it only resolves if the whole
# estate travels together. Admitted at the same time as its workflow below —
# a workflow without its sources is a job that can only fail, which is why
# NECROPHONE's build.yml stays out.
!/PALLBEARER/

# CORONER, the sixth project and the only one that LISTENS rather than making
# sound, joined 2026-11-05. Like the others it depends on ../shared/necromath,
# so it only resolves if the whole estate travels together.
#
# ⚠ READ THIS BEFORE JUDGING ITS CI. Four of CORONER's six harnesses measure
# against NECROPHONE: they lift its real encoder, decoder, parameter registry
# and pitch detector out of its own source and run them unmodified. NECROPHONE
# is NOT in this repository, for the reason stated above its workflow below, so
# on a fresh clone those four have nothing to measure against.
#
# They SKIP rather than fail, and they skip LOUDLY — each prints a banner
# naming exactly what is left unverified, because a silent skip reading as
# green is worse than a red board. Measured on a fresh clone: 2 harnesses run
# (193 checks), 4 announce themselves skipped, everything exits 0. With the
# whole CLAUDE folder present, all six run and 300 checks pass, and THAT is
# the run that counts before a release.
#
# So coroner.yml is admitted below, unlike NECROPHONE's build.yml, because it
# is a job that can succeed honestly rather than one that can only fail.
!/CORONER/

# --- admit the estate's tooling --------------------------------------------
# tools/counts.js derives every live number in the docs from the gates that
# produce them; tools/counts.json is its cache and must be tracked, or CI
# would re-run the slow harnesses on every push.
!/tools/

# --- admit the estate's documents, by exact name ---------------------------
!/AUDIO_INTERCHANGE.md
!/AUTOPSY_ARCHITECTURE.md
!/RIGOR_ARCHITECTURE.md
!/CASKET_ARCHITECTURE.md
!/LICENSE
!/README.md

# --- admit ONLY the estate's workflows -------------------------------------
# NECROPHONE's build.yml also lives in .github/workflows but its sources are
# scattered across the CLAUDE root and NECROPHONE-repo/, neither of which is
# in this repository. Committing it would add a job that could only ever fail.
!/.github/
/.github/*
!/.github/workflows/
/.github/workflows/*
!/.github/workflows/casket.yml
!/.github/workflows/autopsy.yml
!/.github/workflows/rigor.yml
!/.github/workflows/pallbearer.yml
# CORONER's own. Admitted on the same terms as the rest: its sources are in
# this repository. The four gates that need NECROPHONE skip loudly instead of
# failing, so this job reports honestly on what it CAN check rather than
# failing on what it cannot reach. See the CORONER block above.
!/.github/workflows/coroner.yml

# ============================================================================
# Now the ordinary exclusions, applied INSIDE the admitted directories.
# ============================================================================

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------
build/
cmake-build-*/
*.o
*.a
*.dylib
*.so
*.dll
*.exe
*_artefacts/
JUCE/
node_modules/

# --- compiled parity gates (the source is tracked, the binaries are not) ---
core_parity
casket_parity
casket_parity_lto
cp0
cp2
cp3

# --- harness scratch -------------------------------------------------------
# RIGOR's mutation harness writes these while it runs. Committing one would
# capture a deliberately broken core as though it were the real thing.
# WIDENED 2026-08-21. These were `.js`-only, written when the probe tooling
# emitted nothing else. It has since grown .html and .cpp probes, and two of
# them (casket.__probe.html, core_parity.__probe.cpp) reached the index before
# anyone noticed. The rule now covers the extension, whatever it turns out to be.
*.__mut.*
*.__probe.*
.__mut_test.js
*.tailmark
__wtest.txt
__delete_probe_test.js

# --- rendered audio --------------------------------------------------------
# Renders are outputs of the suite, reproducible from the code that made them.
*.wav
*.aiff
*.aif
*.flac
*.mp3

# --- OS and editor ---------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
.~lock.*#

# The Underworld charter (Masterbox↔trilogy boundary law) — admitted to the allowlist
!/UNDERWORLD_CHARTER.md
# ...and its engineering annex (preset schema, build boundary, module collision).
# The charter states the law; this one states the mechanics. Both or neither.
!/UNDERWORLD_INTERCHANGE.md
# The Underworld's own code (the consumer side): spike + translator + diagnostics.
!/underworld/
# The Underworld CI workflow
!/.github/workflows/underworld.yml
